========================
DROPDOWNS IN PLAYWRIGHT
========================

WHAT IS A DROPDOWN?
-------------------

A dropdown is a list of options from which a user can select one or more values.

Example:

Country

▼ India
  USA
  Canada
  Australia

--------------------------------------------------

TYPES OF DROPDOWNS
------------------

1. Standard HTML Dropdown
   Uses <select> tag

2. Custom Dropdown
   Built using div, span, li, etc.

--------------------------------------------------

1. STANDARD HTML DROPDOWN
-------------------------

HTML:

<select id="country">

    <option value="in">India</option>

    <option value="us">USA</option>

    <option value="ca">Canada</option>

</select>

For these dropdowns Playwright provides:

selectOption()

--------------------------------------------------

SELECT BY VISIBLE TEXT
----------------------

await page.locator('#country')
.selectOption({
    label: 'India'
});

Meaning:

Select the option whose text is India.

--------------------------------------------------

SELECT BY VALUE
---------------

HTML:

<option value="in">India</option>

Playwright:

await page.locator('#country')
.selectOption('in');

OR

await page.locator('#country')
.selectOption({
    value: 'in'
});

--------------------------------------------------

SELECT BY INDEX
---------------

await page.locator('#country')
.selectOption({
    index: 0
});

Meaning:

Select first option.

Index starts from 0.

--------------------------------------------------

VERIFY SELECTED VALUE
---------------------

await expect(
    page.locator('#country')
).toHaveValue('in');

--------------------------------------------------

MULTI SELECT DROPDOWN
---------------------

HTML:

<select multiple>

    <option value="java">Java</option>

    <option value="ts">TypeScript</option>

    <option value="python">Python</option>

</select>

Playwright:

await page.locator('#skills')
.selectOption([
    'java',
    'ts'
]);

--------------------------------------------------

CUSTOM DROPDOWN
---------------

Not every dropdown uses <select>.

Many websites create dropdowns using:

div
span
li

Example:

▼ Select Country

After clicking:

India
USA
Canada

--------------------------------------------------

HOW TO HANDLE CUSTOM DROPDOWNS?
-------------------------------

Step 1

Click dropdown.

await page.locator('#country')
.click();

Step 2

Click desired option.

await page.getByText('India')
.click();

--------------------------------------------------

EXAMPLE
-------

await page.locator('.dropdown')
.click();

await page.locator(
    'text=India'
).click();

--------------------------------------------------

HOW TO IDENTIFY DROPDOWN TYPE?
------------------------------

Inspect element.

If you see:

<select>

→ Standard Dropdown

Use:

selectOption()

--------------------------------

If you see:

div
span
li

→ Custom Dropdown

Use:

click()

--------------------------------------------------

COMMON MISTAKES
---------------

Wrong:

await page.locator('.dropdown')
.selectOption('India');

Reason:

Custom dropdown does not support selectOption().

--------------------------------------------------

Correct:

await page.locator('.dropdown')
.click();

await page.getByText('India')
.click();

--------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
-------------------

Q. How do you handle dropdowns in Playwright?

Answer:

For standard dropdowns use:

selectOption()

For custom dropdowns use:

click() and select the option.

--------------------------------------------------

Q. How do you select by text?

Answer:

await locator.selectOption({
    label: 'India'
});

--------------------------------------------------

Q. How do you select by value?

Answer:

await locator.selectOption({
    value: 'in'
});

--------------------------------------------------

Q. How do you select by index?

Answer:

await locator.selectOption({
    index: 0
});

--------------------------------------------------

